from baseline was greater in the sildenafil group (
1.8 \pm -0.7 \text{ mL} \times \text{kg}(-1) \times \text{min}(-1)
) than in the placebo group (
-0.27 \text{ mL} \times \text{kg}(-1) \times \text{min}(-1)
;
P = .02
). Sildenafil reduced pulmonary vascular resistance and increased cardiac output with exercise (
P < .05
vs. placebo for both). Sildenafil improved in 6-minute walk distance (29 m vs. placebo;
P = .047
) and Minnesota Living With Heart Failure score (-14 versus placebo;
P = .01
). Subjects in the sildenafil group experienced fewer hospitalizations for HF

